{"name":"Attorney","hex":"#3f4258","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"attorney","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lawyer; one who advises or represents others in legal matters as a profession.","An agent or representative authorized to act on someone else's behalf in accordance with that person's instructions."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To work as a legal attorney.","To provide with a legal attorney."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attorney"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lawyer","blocks":[{"text":"A lawyer is a person who is qualified to offer advice about the law, draft legal documents, and represent individuals in legal matters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Helena_Normanton.jpg/330px-Helena_Normanton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawyer","wikidata":"Q40348"},{"title":"Attorney at law","blocks":[{"text":"Attorney at law or attorney-at-law, usually abbreviated in everyday speech to attorney, is the preferred term for a practising lawyer in certain jurisdictions, including Poland, South Africa, Sri Lanka, the Philippines, and the United States. The term has its roots in the verb to attorn, meaning to transfer one's rights and obligations to another."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attorney_at_law","wikidata":"Q758225"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg/500px-Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg/1280px-Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg/500px-Juris_Doctor_diploma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th